 ## Background
-Fine-tuning in the context of 3D Gaussian Splatting builds on earlier work in NeRF fine-tuning and generative models. The concept of treating a reconstructed mesh or point cloud as a single-scene NeRF for optimization was introduced in GPN (Generative Point-based NeRF) [S1]. The use of feed-forward models to initialize 3D Gaussians for fine-tuning was later explored in EVolSplat [S3]. The technique is widely used in applications requiring high-fidelity reconstruction of specific objects or scenes, such as virtual reality, cultural heritage preservation, and autonomous driving [S1, S3].
